    Replace Selenium/Python tests with Playwright (#7769)
    
    The Selenium suite (Python, geckodriver, requirements.txt) was the only
    part of this module not on the npm/Vite/TypeScript toolchain used
    everywhere else, making it an extra setup burden for contributors and
    CI. This patch ports it to Playwright:
    
    - tests/mock-server.ts replaces the old MockRequestHandler: serves
    mock-server-api-data/* fixtures directly and proxies everything else to
    the Vite dev server, same as before.
    - tests/global-setup.ts and playwright.config.ts manage the mock server
    and dev server lifecycle, so cleanup no longer depends on every
    assertion succeeding (the old script skipped driver/server teardown on
    the first failed assert).
    - Each of the four original checks becomes an independent Playwright
    test with its own pass/fail result, run against Firefox to match the old
    suite's browser choice.
    
    This updates the GitHub Actions workflow and README accordingly, and
    drops the old Python stuff.
    
    ### How to test this patch
    
    Look at [the GitHub Actions
    run](https://github.com/opencast/opencast/actions/runs/29646424981/job/88085349217?pr=7769)
    or follow the instructions in the README.md.
    
